et_error)\n    251         return doc\n    252 \n\n/System/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/2.6/lib/python2.6/encodings/utf_8.pyc in decode(input, errors)\n     14 \n     15 def decode(input, errors='strict'):\n---> 16     return codecs.utf_8_decode(input, errors, True)\n     17 \n     18 class IncrementalEncoder(codecs.IncrementalEncoder):\n\nUnicodeDecodeError: 'utf8' codec can't decode bytes in position 0-3: invalid data\n```\n\nThis means that the content is not valid UTF-8 despite the webserver telling so:\n\n```\n$ curl -i -X HEAD http://habrahabr.ru/\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nServer: nginx\nDate: Mon, 03 Sep 2012 11:34:16 GMT\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8\nConnection: keep-alive\nKeep-Alive: timeout=25\n```\n\nI don't speak russian but if you can write a python program that decodes the data into a correct python unicode object (possibly filtering encoding errors from the website) then you should be able to use the `CountVectorizer` on that data.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/comments/8236170/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ogrisel","id":89061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5MDYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel","html_url":"https://github.com/ogrisel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ogrisel/repos","eve